1
00:00:00,586 --> 00:00:01,986
(Episode 21)

2
00:00:18,372 --> 00:00:19,872
There are no signs of foul play in the vehicle.

3
00:00:20,312 --> 00:00:21,312
And the doors were locked.

4
00:00:21,412 --> 00:00:23,412
- Any signs of a break-in? - None so far.

5
00:00:23,742 --> 00:00:26,512
Check the CCTV in the area and the dashcam first.

6
00:00:26,582 --> 00:00:28,352
- Yes, sir. - What about the family?

7
00:00:28,552 --> 00:00:29,552
We're working on it.

8
00:00:31,082 --> 00:00:33,952
Detective, I think there's something on the dashboard.

9
00:00:34,622 --> 00:00:35,752
What is it? Bring it here.

10
00:00:36,392 --> 00:00:40,062
(Detective, Police)

11
00:00:41,662 --> 00:00:42,662
I think it's a suicide note.

12
00:00:43,132 --> 00:00:44,132
A suicide note?

13
00:00:45,902 --> 00:00:50,272
(To Ko Eun Seol)

14
00:00:50,872 --> 00:00:52,602
Mom, Dad, it's bad!

15
00:00:52,672 --> 00:00:53,872
They're saying Manager Na is dead!

16
00:00:59,112 --> 00:01:01,652
What? What are you talking about? Who died?

17
00:01:01,752 --> 00:01:04,022
Manager Na, the company's PR manager.

18
00:01:04,252 --> 00:01:06,692
Why him? Why did he die?

19
00:01:07,092 --> 00:01:09,022
They said he took his own life in his car.

20
00:01:09,192 --> 00:01:11,222
Oh, my goodness. My gosh!

21
00:01:12,022 --> 00:01:13,092
Who said that?

22
00:01:14,192 --> 00:01:15,432
I got a call from the company.

23
00:01:15,592 --> 00:01:17,262
The police are checking with the company too.

24
00:01:17,332 --> 00:01:19,602
So, why did he do it?

25
00:01:20,032 --> 00:01:22,702
I don't know. But they said they found a suicide note.

26
00:01:23,272 --> 00:01:24,272
A suicide note?

27
00:01:24,472 --> 00:01:26,572
- Yes. - I need to head to the office.

28
00:01:26,642 --> 00:01:28,172
Yes, you should do that.

29
00:01:28,242 --> 00:01:29,242
This is terrible.

30
00:01:30,242 --> 00:01:31,242
I can't believe this.

31
00:01:32,312 --> 00:01:36,012
Now, Ko Eun Seol, what will you do?

32
00:01:36,452 --> 00:01:40,792
(Violent Crimes Unit 2)

33
00:01:41,752 --> 00:01:43,192
Did you have any personal contact...

34
00:01:43,862 --> 00:01:45,422
with Na Tae Hoon recently?

35
00:01:47,492 --> 00:01:48,492
Yes.

36
00:01:48,992 --> 00:01:50,062
Why did you meet?

37
00:01:50,662 --> 00:01:53,002
Regarding my case from ten years ago,

38
00:01:54,502 --> 00:01:56,472
I had something to confirm.

39
00:01:57,042 --> 00:01:58,742
What connection do you think there was?

40
00:02:01,572 --> 00:02:03,182
I thought he might be the one...

41
00:02:05,342 --> 00:02:09,012
who bribed Lee Jung Tae to commit perjury.

42
00:02:10,352 --> 00:02:11,582
Do you have any proof?

43
00:02:12,582 --> 00:02:14,022
There are several pieces of circumstantial evidence.

44
00:02:14,522 --> 00:02:16,122
We will submit the necessary documents.

45
00:02:16,352 --> 00:02:19,662
Did you, by any chance, threaten or blackmail Na Tae Hoon...

46
00:02:20,162 --> 00:02:22,062
in relation to this?

47
00:02:26,202 --> 00:02:28,332
Detective, what kind of nonsense...

48
00:02:31,572 --> 00:02:32,572
Ms. Ko?

49
00:02:39,412 --> 00:02:40,412
Detective.

50
00:02:46,952 --> 00:02:50,562
Na Tae Hoon left a suicide note for you.

51
00:02:52,662 --> 00:02:53,832
For me?

52
00:03:10,782 --> 00:03:12,182
Ms. Joo, what brings you here?

53
00:03:15,012 --> 00:03:16,282
Since I'm in charge of the department,

54
00:03:16,282 --> 00:03:17,982
I was called in for questioning.

55
00:03:27,692 --> 00:03:30,162
Ms. Ko, are you okay?

56
00:03:33,402 --> 00:03:36,272
Yes, I'm fine.

57
00:03:37,302 --> 00:03:39,572
You must be shocked about Manager Na.

58
00:03:46,342 --> 00:03:48,782
I just heard they found a suicide note.

59
00:03:51,652 --> 00:03:52,752
Ms. Joo...

60
00:03:53,722 --> 00:03:57,262
Right. I guess now isn't the time to ask.

61
00:03:58,492 --> 00:03:59,492
I'm sorry.

62
00:04:02,432 --> 00:04:04,662
Ms. Ko, please come this way.

63
00:04:58,782 --> 00:05:00,992
Do you want me to read it for you?

64
00:05:02,822 --> 00:05:03,822
No.

65
00:05:05,892 --> 00:05:07,332
I'll read it myself.

66
00:05:23,812 --> 00:05:25,082
To Ko Eun Seol.

67
00:05:26,142 --> 00:05:27,752
If you are reading this,

68
00:05:28,652 --> 00:05:31,182
I'm probably no longer in this world.

69
00:05:32,482 --> 00:05:33,892
That day, ten years ago,

70
00:05:34,792 --> 00:05:36,762
the person who killed your mother...

71
00:05:37,492 --> 00:05:38,722
was me.

72
00:05:41,732 --> 00:05:42,732
What's wrong, Eun Seol?

73
00:05:43,662 --> 00:05:44,702
What does it say?

74
00:05:51,142 --> 00:05:53,302
The one who actually killed my mom...

75
00:05:55,372 --> 00:05:57,142
He says it was Manager Na himself.

76
00:05:58,542 --> 00:06:00,012
What? What did you say?

77
00:06:03,482 --> 00:06:06,822
That day, I had just finalised my divorce,

78
00:06:07,552 --> 00:06:09,152
and I was not in my right mind.

79
00:06:10,522 --> 00:06:12,192
I had also been drinking,

80
00:06:12,662 --> 00:06:16,192
and I got into a petty argument with your mother over parking.

81
00:06:17,162 --> 00:06:18,832
I couldn't control my temper,

82
00:06:19,532 --> 00:06:21,972
so I followed her and pushed her.

83
00:06:23,202 --> 00:06:26,102
And that's how she died.

84
00:06:27,712 --> 00:06:29,942
It all happened in an instant.

85
00:06:31,512 --> 00:06:32,982
Ever since the day I ran away,

86
00:06:33,482 --> 00:06:36,312
I haven't had a single peaceful night's sleep.

87
00:06:37,352 --> 00:06:39,552
I tried to get by with alcohol to forget,

88
00:06:40,652 --> 00:06:41,692
but from the moment...

89
00:06:42,222 --> 00:06:44,462
you appeared before me,

90
00:06:44,862 --> 00:06:47,062
I knew it was all over.

91
00:06:48,292 --> 00:06:51,962
I no longer have the nerve to hide, nor the courage to go to prison.

92
00:06:53,362 --> 00:06:57,702
By dying, I beg for forgiveness from you and your mother.

93
00:06:58,802 --> 00:06:59,802
I'm sorry.

94
00:07:00,442 --> 00:07:01,542
Na Tae Hoon.

95
00:07:06,812 --> 00:07:09,382
This can't be. No...

96
00:07:11,222 --> 00:07:12,222
Eun Seol.

97
00:07:14,352 --> 00:07:15,422
A petty...

98
00:07:17,462 --> 00:07:19,892
He said it was a petty dispute over parking.

99
00:07:25,002 --> 00:07:26,502
While he was drunk...

100
00:07:27,602 --> 00:07:30,542
He just pushed her because he was drunk.

101
00:07:34,442 --> 00:07:35,542
A dispute over parking?

102
00:07:37,142 --> 00:07:39,742
For a ridiculous reason like that,

103
00:07:39,942 --> 00:07:41,612
he took a person's life...

104
00:07:41,952 --> 00:07:45,082
and let you be framed as a murderer for ten years?

105
00:07:46,152 --> 00:07:47,392
Mom...

106
00:07:48,552 --> 00:07:51,592
My poor mom. It's so unfair.

107
00:08:04,872 --> 00:08:06,402
Mom...

108
00:08:13,682 --> 00:08:15,382
My gosh!

109
00:08:17,652 --> 00:08:20,352
He killed Mom over a mere parking dispute?

110
00:08:21,222 --> 00:08:23,592
And then killed himself because he couldn't handle it?

111
00:08:24,422 --> 00:08:26,722
Darn it. I should've killed that punk...

112
00:08:26,822 --> 00:08:29,362
or at least broken one of his bones.

113
00:08:30,132 --> 00:08:31,962
What a horrible thing to say.

114
00:08:32,762 --> 00:08:34,332
Do you want to end up in prison?

115
00:08:34,402 --> 00:08:35,732
Grandma, are you saying...

116
00:08:36,102 --> 00:08:38,472
that we should let the punk who killed Mom and framed Eun Seol...

117
00:08:38,602 --> 00:08:40,612
get off so meaninglessly?

118
00:08:40,672 --> 00:08:42,112
Who said that?

119
00:08:43,212 --> 00:08:45,842
If I had at least spat in that punk's face,

120
00:08:45,912 --> 00:08:47,112
I'd feel less bitter.

121
00:08:48,282 --> 00:08:51,882
Not being able to is my life's greatest regret.

122
00:08:52,622 --> 00:08:54,692
What good would spitting do?

123
00:08:54,952 --> 00:08:57,962
Just be glad that Eun Seol was exonerated.

124
00:08:58,422 --> 00:09:00,892
What would we have done if not for that?

125
00:09:03,062 --> 00:09:04,202
Of course.

126
00:09:04,802 --> 00:09:06,802
I guess you're right.

127
00:09:07,472 --> 00:09:10,272
Darn, this is driving me crazy!

128
00:09:13,042 --> 00:09:15,072
Are you going off to cause trouble again?

129
00:09:15,872 --> 00:09:18,482
Hey, don't just sit there. Go stop Eun Guk.

130
00:09:18,712 --> 00:09:22,412
Just leave him be. He must be furious to act like that.

131
00:09:25,552 --> 00:09:27,922
The police found no signs of a forced entry,

132
00:09:27,992 --> 00:09:29,322
and since a suicide note was left behind,

133
00:09:29,392 --> 00:09:30,792
they are ruling it a suicide...

134
00:09:30,862 --> 00:09:32,922
and are investigating the exact circumstances.

135
00:09:33,262 --> 00:09:35,432
Meanwhile, the note left by Mr. Na...

136
00:09:35,492 --> 00:09:38,402
reportedly contains a shocking confession...

137
00:09:38,462 --> 00:09:41,372
about the murder of a woman ten years ago.

138
00:09:41,632 --> 00:09:44,502
In the note, he states that he is the real killer...

139
00:09:44,572 --> 00:09:47,212
and that he framed the victim's daughter, Ms. Ko,

140
00:09:47,272 --> 00:09:50,342
for her own mother's murder.

141
00:09:50,412 --> 00:09:52,142
Legal experts say this greatly increases...

142
00:09:52,142 --> 00:09:53,852
the chances of a retrial for Ms. Ko,

143
00:09:53,912 --> 00:09:57,122
who was wrongly imprisoned for ten years.

144
00:09:57,522 --> 00:09:58,522
(Planning Director, Cha Seok Jin)

145
00:10:04,222 --> 00:10:05,222
Seok Jin, what's up?

146
00:10:06,122 --> 00:10:07,662
Nothing really.

147
00:10:08,662 --> 00:10:10,292
Why do you look so serious?

148
00:10:10,362 --> 00:10:11,632
Is it because of Manager Na?

149
00:10:13,302 --> 00:10:14,302
You know...

150
00:10:14,602 --> 00:10:16,232
Now that I think about it, Ko Eun Seol must've...

151
00:10:16,302 --> 00:10:19,702
wormed her way into our company to find the killer.

152
00:10:20,242 --> 00:10:23,642
In the end, the killer was caught, so hasn't she achieved her goal?

153
00:10:25,682 --> 00:10:27,852
You want to call that achieving her goal?

154
00:10:28,782 --> 00:10:30,822
- No, I just meant... - Kang Hae Ra.

155
00:10:32,082 --> 00:10:33,482
Someone died.

156
00:10:34,522 --> 00:10:37,722
And Eun Seol just found out today that the real killer of the crime...

157
00:10:37,792 --> 00:10:39,922
she spent ten years taking the blame for has died.

158
00:10:40,662 --> 00:10:41,692
So?

159
00:10:41,992 --> 00:10:44,732
Just for today, don't say anything bad about her.

160
00:10:48,602 --> 00:10:50,472
I need to work, so could you please leave?

161
00:10:57,412 --> 00:10:59,542
(Cheongma Scholarship Foundation, Chairman Kim Jung Sun)

162
00:10:59,642 --> 00:11:01,082
What's this?

163
00:11:02,382 --> 00:11:04,082
I'll take moral responsibility for Manager Na's death...

164
00:11:04,152 --> 00:11:05,822
and step down, ma'am.

165
00:11:06,752 --> 00:11:08,322
Taking moral responsibility...

166
00:11:08,392 --> 00:11:10,522
doesn't require a letter of resignation.

167
00:11:11,122 --> 00:11:12,422
Put it away.

168
00:11:12,722 --> 00:11:14,362
Please just accept it.

169
00:11:14,432 --> 00:11:17,302
Don't you know I need you by my side, Director Joo?

170
00:11:17,602 --> 00:11:19,432
I said put it away.

171
00:11:23,432 --> 00:11:24,442
Yes, ma'am.

172
00:11:25,342 --> 00:11:26,342
Then...

173
00:11:28,342 --> 00:11:29,812
Anyway,

174
00:11:30,512 --> 00:11:33,642
I'm just so relieved that Eun Seol has been exonerated.

175
00:11:34,082 --> 00:11:36,952
I should meet up with her and offer my sympathies.

176
00:11:38,082 --> 00:11:39,082
Your sympathies?

177
00:11:39,252 --> 00:11:40,552
Or should I congratulate her?

178
00:11:41,122 --> 00:11:43,522
Whichever it is, I'll take care of it...

179
00:11:43,552 --> 00:11:45,062
and deliver the condolence money.

180
00:11:45,692 --> 00:11:47,832
You do it on behalf of the company, Director Joo.

181
00:11:48,032 --> 00:11:49,892
I'll do it on a personal level.

182
00:11:50,602 --> 00:11:52,562
As you know, Director Joo, Eun Seol and I...

183
00:11:52,632 --> 00:11:54,332
share a special connection.

184
00:11:55,502 --> 00:11:56,572
Of course.

185
00:11:57,002 --> 00:11:58,672
The connection is definitely special.

186
00:12:05,382 --> 00:12:06,782
Sympathies, my foot.

187
00:12:07,952 --> 00:12:10,182
Always pretending to be the kindest person on earth.

188
00:12:17,092 --> 00:12:18,122
What was that?

189
00:12:18,362 --> 00:12:20,292
Director Joo tendered her resignation?

190
00:12:20,292 --> 00:12:21,362
Exactly.

191
00:12:23,432 --> 00:12:25,562
So? Did you accept it?

192
00:12:25,732 --> 00:12:28,132
Are you crazy? Why would I accept it?

193
00:12:28,202 --> 00:12:30,102
What would I do without Director Joo?

194
00:12:30,972 --> 00:12:31,972
Honey,

195
00:12:32,042 --> 00:12:34,512
don't you think you rely too much on her?

196
00:12:35,342 --> 00:12:37,412
Do you know how good she is to me?

197
00:12:37,482 --> 00:12:39,212
Isn't it only natural that I rely on her?

198
00:12:39,282 --> 00:12:42,512
Yes, and that is textbook gaslighting.

199
00:12:43,152 --> 00:12:44,752
Gaslighting? Don't be ridiculous.

200
00:12:45,782 --> 00:12:48,092
As long as it makes my life easier, who cares?

201
00:12:50,862 --> 00:12:51,892
By the way,

202
00:12:52,862 --> 00:12:55,792
has Director Joo ever told us about her family?

203
00:12:56,192 --> 00:12:59,032
Her parents passed away young, and she has one brother...

204
00:12:59,262 --> 00:13:00,702
who lives in the US.

205
00:13:01,572 --> 00:13:05,172
How is it that you know absolutely nothing about her?

206
00:13:05,802 --> 00:13:07,872
Is there any reason I should know?

207
00:13:08,642 --> 00:13:11,142
Director Joo would be sad to hear that.

208
00:13:31,402 --> 00:13:32,402
Hee Jung.

209
00:13:34,032 --> 00:13:36,902
You know I'm not much of a drinker.

210
00:13:40,812 --> 00:13:42,372
But I feel like having a drink today.

211
00:13:50,822 --> 00:13:51,882
I'm sorry.

212
00:13:55,452 --> 00:13:56,752
I'm so sorry, Hee Jung.

213
00:14:00,422 --> 00:14:01,862
I'm sorry to you...

214
00:14:04,532 --> 00:14:06,132
and I'm sorry to Eun Seol.

215
00:14:56,552 --> 00:14:57,582
Eun Seol.

216
00:15:00,822 --> 00:15:02,622
- Mom. - Here, let me carry your bag.

217
00:15:02,692 --> 00:15:05,392
- It's okay. - At least let me take this.

218
00:15:09,032 --> 00:15:10,462
Do you enjoy painting?

219
00:15:11,262 --> 00:15:12,262
Yes.

220
00:15:13,662 --> 00:15:16,302
So you want to go to art school?

221
00:15:16,672 --> 00:15:17,772
Could you afford to send me?

222
00:15:21,172 --> 00:15:24,282
If you want to go, then of course I'll send you.

223
00:15:25,242 --> 00:15:28,912
It's okay. I know you're already stretched thin supporting Eun Guk.

224
00:15:29,782 --> 00:15:31,352
I can just paint as a hobby.

225
00:15:34,192 --> 00:15:36,392
There's no need to look at me like that.

226
00:15:37,592 --> 00:15:39,062
I feel bad, that's all.

227
00:15:39,962 --> 00:15:43,162
I'm a parent who can't even properly support her own child.

228
00:15:44,962 --> 00:15:46,332
You have nothing to be sorry for.

229
00:15:47,062 --> 00:15:48,072
Anyway, Mom,

230
00:15:48,402 --> 00:15:50,742
I'm hungry. Is there anything to eat at home?

231
00:15:51,902 --> 00:15:54,542
As a matter of fact, I made your favourite, tteokbokki.

232
00:15:55,042 --> 00:15:56,112
Sounds delicious.

233
00:15:57,172 --> 00:15:58,182
It'll be spicy.

234
00:16:08,652 --> 00:16:10,452
Mom...

235
00:16:12,362 --> 00:16:13,692
Mom, today, I really...

236
00:16:13,792 --> 00:16:15,692
I miss you so, so much.

237
00:16:17,262 --> 00:16:19,102
Just one more time...

238
00:16:20,162 --> 00:16:22,672
Just one more time...

239
00:16:23,202 --> 00:16:25,802
I just want to see you one more time, Mom.

240
00:17:05,612 --> 00:17:06,612
Here. Use this.

241
00:17:09,212 --> 00:17:10,252
Thank you.

242
00:17:14,322 --> 00:17:15,752
Are you feeling a little better now?

243
00:17:21,862 --> 00:17:23,262
I heard it was over a parking dispute.

244
00:17:24,162 --> 00:17:25,732
The reason your mother passed away, I mean.

245
00:17:30,072 --> 00:17:31,802
But I just can't believe it.

246
00:17:33,572 --> 00:17:36,172
How could someone take a life over something so small?

247
00:17:39,112 --> 00:17:40,412
And Manager Na...

248
00:17:41,812 --> 00:17:45,052
I also can't believe he took his own life.

249
00:17:48,092 --> 00:17:49,792
Above all, this whole thing...

250
00:17:51,022 --> 00:17:53,562
feels like my fault, and it weighs heavily on me.

251
00:17:55,092 --> 00:17:57,602
Don't say that. Why is any of this your fault?

252
00:17:59,102 --> 00:18:00,302
Late as it was,

253
00:18:00,362 --> 00:18:02,302
he probably felt he had to pay for his sins.

254
00:18:05,272 --> 00:18:06,272
But...

255
00:18:07,942 --> 00:18:10,912
I don't really know what kind of person Manager Na was.

256
00:18:12,712 --> 00:18:13,742
In his note,

257
00:18:13,912 --> 00:18:18,322
he said he knew it was over the moment I appeared.

258
00:18:20,382 --> 00:18:22,852
But the Manager Na I saw wasn't like that.

259
00:18:24,662 --> 00:18:25,822
What do you mean by that?

260
00:18:27,462 --> 00:18:30,262
He didn't seem like someone who had accepted it all.

261
00:18:31,932 --> 00:18:34,672
He was desperately trying to cover it up more than anyone.

262
00:18:37,842 --> 00:18:38,842
And more importantly,

263
00:18:39,672 --> 00:18:42,842
my mom wasn't the type to get into a fight over a parking spot.

264
00:18:43,772 --> 00:18:45,382
Also, where my mom died...

265
00:18:45,682 --> 00:18:47,682
has no connection to her at all.

266
00:18:47,752 --> 00:18:49,252
She had no reason to be there.

267
00:18:51,822 --> 00:18:53,122
No matter how I think about it,

268
00:18:53,782 --> 00:18:56,252
there's just no connection between Manager Na and my mom.

269
00:18:56,622 --> 00:18:59,422
You're saying someone else was behind the murder?

270
00:19:01,562 --> 00:19:04,262
Then why would Manager Na choose to take his own life?

271
00:19:06,602 --> 00:19:07,972
I don't know.

272
00:19:08,932 --> 00:19:11,002
Right now, I don't have the energy to think about it.

273
00:19:14,772 --> 00:19:15,812
By the way,

274
00:19:16,572 --> 00:19:18,842
what are you doing here?

275
00:19:22,882 --> 00:19:25,352
I was worried, so I went to your house.

276
00:19:26,452 --> 00:19:27,482
Then I followed you.

277
00:19:29,352 --> 00:19:30,992
To my house?

278
00:19:31,492 --> 00:19:32,492
Yes.

279
00:19:37,662 --> 00:19:39,902
You know, even after all this time,

280
00:19:39,962 --> 00:19:41,432
this place hasn't changed a bit.

281
00:19:49,942 --> 00:19:51,242
Did you know?

282
00:19:53,442 --> 00:19:55,112
I came back to Korea...

283
00:19:55,782 --> 00:19:58,022
for a little while once, just to find you.

284
00:20:02,792 --> 00:20:03,792
No.

285
00:20:05,222 --> 00:20:06,422
You did?

286
00:20:07,862 --> 00:20:10,262
I couldn't get through to you on your phone or by email.

287
00:20:11,002 --> 00:20:12,462
It was driving me crazy.

288
00:20:13,462 --> 00:20:14,932
I wanted to at least know the reason,

289
00:20:15,002 --> 00:20:16,732
so I came back for a short while.

290
00:20:31,782 --> 00:20:32,782
Ko Eun Seol...

291
00:20:36,752 --> 00:20:38,962
(Ko Gi Han)

292
00:20:39,022 --> 00:20:40,622
Gosh, hello.

293
00:20:41,092 --> 00:20:42,192
Who are you?

294
00:20:42,462 --> 00:20:45,102
I'm an upper classman from Eun Seol's school.

295
00:20:45,162 --> 00:20:47,032
I haven't been able to get in touch with her,

296
00:20:47,162 --> 00:20:48,602
so I was wondering if she's home.

297
00:20:49,332 --> 00:20:51,002
Eun Seol isn't here.

298
00:20:51,642 --> 00:20:53,102
Then where did she go?

299
00:20:53,442 --> 00:20:57,712
Don't ask any more questions. I don't even want to say her name.

300
00:20:57,982 --> 00:21:00,382
What do you mean by that? Why? What happened?

301
00:21:00,442 --> 00:21:02,052
I told you not to ask.

302
00:21:03,212 --> 00:21:04,752
Ma'am!

303
00:21:14,432 --> 00:21:17,262
(Ko Gi Han)

304
00:21:43,292 --> 00:21:45,762
I really looked everywhere for you back then.

305
00:21:51,402 --> 00:21:53,132
I needed to know why you cut off contact,

306
00:21:54,972 --> 00:21:58,102
and if I had done something wrong. I just had to know.

307
00:21:59,802 --> 00:22:00,802
Back then...

308
00:22:03,212 --> 00:22:05,042
I couldn't contact you.

309
00:22:06,442 --> 00:22:07,682
I know that now.

310
00:22:10,912 --> 00:22:11,952
But...

311
00:22:14,282 --> 00:22:15,822
I was a little resentful.

312
00:22:19,622 --> 00:22:21,362
You just disappeared without a word.

313
00:22:27,832 --> 00:22:28,902
I'm sorry.

314
00:22:31,642 --> 00:22:33,472
I'm not saying this to get an apology.

315
00:22:33,542 --> 00:22:34,612
It's just...

316
00:22:36,242 --> 00:22:38,912
I felt like you should know.

317
00:22:53,562 --> 00:22:55,732
Why call a meeting so early in the morning?

318
00:22:58,032 --> 00:22:59,462
All right, everyone.

319
00:22:59,762 --> 00:23:01,572
As the head of this family,

320
00:23:02,002 --> 00:23:03,732
I've gathered you all to say something.

321
00:23:04,872 --> 00:23:06,142
First, Eun Seol...

322
00:23:07,342 --> 00:23:09,772
You've been through so much.

323
00:23:10,672 --> 00:23:14,552
I'm sorry you had to do what Eun Guk and I should've done.

324
00:23:14,552 --> 00:23:16,312
Why was it only your job?

325
00:23:16,612 --> 00:23:17,922
Am I not Mom's daughter too?

326
00:23:17,952 --> 00:23:20,252
No, that's not what I meant.

327
00:23:21,452 --> 00:23:23,222
I know what you mean, Dad.

328
00:23:23,792 --> 00:23:25,592
- You get it, right? - Of course.

329
00:23:27,322 --> 00:23:28,392
Ko Eun Seol.

330
00:23:29,392 --> 00:23:30,592
Let me apologize again.

331
00:23:31,702 --> 00:23:34,572
I'm so sorry that I ever misunderstood you.

332
00:23:34,972 --> 00:23:37,572
You don't have to. It's all in the past now.

333
00:23:39,002 --> 00:23:40,002
From now on,

334
00:23:40,002 --> 00:23:41,642
I'm going to get serious and work hard.

335
00:23:41,712 --> 00:23:44,542
Eun Guk, stop just talking about your business idea.

336
00:23:44,612 --> 00:23:46,942
If you're going to start something, get to it already.

337
00:23:47,182 --> 00:23:49,412
How long are you going to let her be the only one making money?

338
00:23:49,782 --> 00:23:51,182
That's already the plan.

339
00:23:53,022 --> 00:23:54,052
Just give me a little more time.

340
00:23:55,352 --> 00:23:56,522
Okay, and...

341
00:23:58,692 --> 00:24:00,722
From today on, Mom, you're in charge of the housework.

342
00:24:01,162 --> 00:24:02,692
If the three of us are earning money,

343
00:24:02,692 --> 00:24:05,632
it only makes sense for you to manage the house, right?

344
00:24:05,902 --> 00:24:07,902
I'm old enough to give up what little I already do,

345
00:24:07,972 --> 00:24:09,802
and you want me to take on more?

346
00:24:10,332 --> 00:24:11,702
Go make a lot of money...

347
00:24:11,772 --> 00:24:14,002
and hire a housekeeper like you used to.

348
00:24:14,342 --> 00:24:16,172
- What? - I'm hungry.

349
00:24:16,172 --> 00:24:17,842
Enough with the speeches. Let's just have breakfast.

350
00:24:18,442 --> 00:24:19,542
I'm starving.

351
00:24:33,692 --> 00:24:35,362
How does it feel to have your name cleared?

352
00:24:36,862 --> 00:24:38,302
Well, I'm not sure.

353
00:24:39,102 --> 00:24:42,132
It's still a bit surreal. It hasn't really sunk in yet.

354
00:24:42,532 --> 00:24:44,542
But was it really Manager Na?

355
00:24:45,242 --> 00:24:47,002
Are you sure you were framed?

356
00:24:48,572 --> 00:24:51,882
You still want me to be a murderer, don't you?

357
00:24:52,842 --> 00:24:54,082
It's not that.

358
00:24:55,312 --> 00:24:58,182
Anyway, looks like you've achieved your goal,

359
00:24:58,182 --> 00:24:59,552
so how about you get lost?

360
00:24:59,782 --> 00:25:01,022
What's that supposed to mean?

361
00:25:01,392 --> 00:25:03,892
You came to this company to catch the killer, right?

362
00:25:03,952 --> 00:25:05,162
And you caught him.

363
00:25:05,892 --> 00:25:07,292
So you can leave now, can't you?

364
00:25:09,432 --> 00:25:10,432
No.

365
00:25:10,932 --> 00:25:12,862
In fact, I plan on working very hard here.

366
00:25:13,132 --> 00:25:14,132
What?

367
00:25:15,272 --> 00:25:18,242
I still have my retrial, and I need to catch Lee Jung Tae.

368
00:25:18,772 --> 00:25:20,142
And most importantly,

369
00:25:20,672 --> 00:25:23,812
I got into the Cheongma based on my skills, remember?

370
00:25:26,912 --> 00:25:29,412
Now that I'll be able to clear my name,

371
00:25:29,852 --> 00:25:32,422
I'm going to show you what I can really do.

372
00:25:33,822 --> 00:25:37,722
So you'd better look forward to it, Ms. Kang.

373
00:25:43,032 --> 00:25:44,492
For this shoe launch,

374
00:25:44,492 --> 00:25:48,132
I believe we must exclusively target the high-end niche market.

375
00:25:48,532 --> 00:25:49,532
To break the perception...

376
00:25:49,532 --> 00:25:51,742
that functional shoes are clunky and outdated,

377
00:25:51,902 --> 00:25:54,842
we should pair our technology with an Italian workshop collaboration...

378
00:25:55,012 --> 00:25:56,812
and position them as luxury footwear.

379
00:25:57,012 --> 00:25:58,612
Healthy footwear...

380
00:25:58,682 --> 00:26:00,782
that also has premium collectible value?

381
00:26:01,082 --> 00:26:02,712
That is bound to create buzz...

382
00:26:02,712 --> 00:26:04,412
and positively impact our brand image.

383
00:26:04,822 --> 00:26:06,882
But an excessively high pricing strategy...

384
00:26:07,452 --> 00:26:09,852
can be an obstacle for our initial market entry.

385
00:26:10,392 --> 00:26:12,092
The core customer base for functional shoes...

386
00:26:12,092 --> 00:26:13,922
is middle-aged people and the general public.

387
00:26:13,922 --> 00:26:15,432
If we go beyond their price point,

388
00:26:15,662 --> 00:26:17,492
the technology won't matter because...

389
00:26:17,792 --> 00:26:19,132
it'll be entirely out of their reach.

390
00:26:19,332 --> 00:26:23,102
That is the essence of demarketing and scarcity value, Ms. Ko.

391
00:26:23,632 --> 00:26:26,142
A brand's value isn't determined by its price tag.

392
00:26:26,202 --> 00:26:28,112
I believe it comes from...

393
00:26:28,112 --> 00:26:30,212
genuine consumer trust and product experience.

394
00:26:30,842 --> 00:26:32,782
If the core of the technology is foot health,

395
00:26:32,782 --> 00:26:34,312
a reasonable pricing policy...

396
00:26:34,312 --> 00:26:36,212
that lets the general public experience it...

397
00:26:36,512 --> 00:26:39,152
will build true brand loyalty for Cheongma.

398
00:26:40,152 --> 00:26:41,592
The purpose of a corporation...

399
00:26:41,592 --> 00:26:43,952
is to maximize profit, not to be a charity.

400
00:26:44,092 --> 00:26:46,292
Targeting high-end customers with proven spending power,

401
00:26:46,292 --> 00:26:48,162
even if it narrows our demographic,

402
00:26:48,362 --> 00:26:50,192
is a much smarter sales strategy.

403
00:26:50,632 --> 00:26:52,532
(Cheongma)

404
00:26:59,102 --> 00:27:00,972
Your tea is getting cold. Please, drink.

405
00:27:01,672 --> 00:27:02,672
Right.

406
00:27:10,652 --> 00:27:13,582
Was there a particular reason you wanted to see me?

407
00:27:15,752 --> 00:27:17,522
I called you here because of Manager Na.

408
00:27:19,122 --> 00:27:20,992
An employee who worked under me...

409
00:27:21,832 --> 00:27:23,762
committed such a horrific act,

410
00:27:24,562 --> 00:27:25,562
and then...

411
00:27:25,632 --> 00:27:27,932
to end his own life that way...

412
00:27:28,872 --> 00:27:30,402
Honestly, it's just devastating.

413
00:27:31,302 --> 00:27:32,302
As his supervisor,

414
00:27:32,372 --> 00:27:34,172
I feel a profound sense of moral responsibility.

415
00:27:35,372 --> 00:27:38,112
I don't think it's something you need to apologize for, Ms. Joo.

416
00:27:44,212 --> 00:27:45,822
What's this?

417
00:27:47,482 --> 00:27:49,852
I can't imagine the pain you've endured...

418
00:27:49,922 --> 00:27:51,252
for the past ten years,

419
00:27:51,992 --> 00:27:55,462
but this is an unofficial gesture of compensation from the company,

420
00:27:56,062 --> 00:27:57,792
as well as a personal expression of my condolences.

421
00:28:03,432 --> 00:28:04,802
I appreciate the thought.

422
00:28:05,802 --> 00:28:09,712
But the years I've lost can't be compensated for with money.

423
00:28:13,282 --> 00:28:14,482
Is this pride talking?

424
00:28:15,152 --> 00:28:17,512
It's not pride. It's a matter of principle.

425
00:28:18,452 --> 00:28:20,882
I don't want any sympathy...

426
00:28:21,552 --> 00:28:22,552
or condolences.

427
00:28:25,662 --> 00:28:27,522
You're quite bold, Ms. Ko.

428
00:28:29,162 --> 00:28:30,162
Fine.

429
00:28:30,992 --> 00:28:33,832
Let's just say it was rash of me to think money could fix everything.

430
00:28:34,532 --> 00:28:37,902
Instead, feel free to call in a favour from me anytime.

431
00:28:39,042 --> 00:28:41,272
I'll consider myself in your debt on behalf of Manager Na.

432
00:28:42,042 --> 00:28:43,472
I appreciate the offer,

433
00:28:44,072 --> 00:28:46,582
but that will never happen.

434
00:28:47,642 --> 00:28:49,782
Why not? Isn't this all over?

435
00:28:50,682 --> 00:28:52,122
There's still the retrial,

436
00:28:52,452 --> 00:28:53,882
and I still have to catch Lee Jung Tae.

437
00:28:54,792 --> 00:28:56,792
I have to see this through to the end.

438
00:28:59,622 --> 00:29:01,662
All right. You may go.

439
00:29:02,332 --> 00:29:04,232
You must be busy with the shoe brand launch.

440
00:29:17,542 --> 00:29:18,782
You insolent little girl.

441
00:29:19,482 --> 00:29:21,282
What? A matter of principle?

442
00:29:22,452 --> 00:29:23,952
She doesn't know her place.

443
00:29:28,822 --> 00:29:30,522
I guess it's time to take care of this.

444
00:29:36,692 --> 00:29:38,532
I thought you were going to start working hard today.

445
00:29:38,602 --> 00:29:39,762
What are you doing here?

446
00:29:42,402 --> 00:29:45,302
I decided to rest today and start tomorrow.

447
00:29:45,772 --> 00:29:47,272
I knew it.

448
00:29:47,842 --> 00:29:49,172
I've heard of resolutions...

449
00:29:49,242 --> 00:29:51,272
lasting three days, but not half a day.

450
00:29:51,982 --> 00:29:54,582
Come on, I told you I'll work hard starting tomorrow.

451
00:29:54,852 --> 00:29:56,052
As if.

452
00:29:56,982 --> 00:29:59,452
What's with that shabby-looking box?

453
00:29:59,882 --> 00:30:02,022
It belonged to Hee Jung.

454
00:30:04,292 --> 00:30:07,262
After she died so unjustly...

455
00:30:07,892 --> 00:30:10,332
and Eun Seol was taken away,

456
00:30:11,392 --> 00:30:12,862
I was so heartbroken...

457
00:30:13,732 --> 00:30:16,402
that I couldn't bear to look at it, so I shoved it in the closet.

458
00:30:16,932 --> 00:30:19,572
But now that the killer has been revealed...

459
00:30:20,342 --> 00:30:21,572
and Hee Jung can finally rest in peace,

460
00:30:22,172 --> 00:30:24,942
I was going to look through it, then burn it at the temple.

461
00:30:25,912 --> 00:30:28,782
Why would you burn it without even knowing what's inside?

462
00:30:29,812 --> 00:30:30,812
Go on, open it.

463
00:30:32,522 --> 00:30:34,652
What if there are some valuables in there?

464
00:30:34,922 --> 00:30:36,222
Mom, please.

465
00:30:36,722 --> 00:30:38,462
Come on, hurry and open it.

466
00:30:47,202 --> 00:30:49,372
Seriously? Where are the valuables?

467
00:30:49,972 --> 00:30:51,532
Why is there only this sort of stuff in here?

468
00:30:52,042 --> 00:30:55,442
That's Hee Jung for you. She loved her children so much.

469
00:30:55,742 --> 00:30:56,812
Hey, wait a second.

470
00:30:57,442 --> 00:30:59,412
- What's this? - Let's see.

471
00:30:59,812 --> 00:31:01,482
This is a maternity handbook.

472
00:31:01,982 --> 00:31:03,512
Well, open it up.

473
00:31:05,322 --> 00:31:06,922
Let's see. What did she write?

474
00:31:08,422 --> 00:31:09,422
Joo Ae Sook?

475
00:31:10,492 --> 00:31:11,592
Who's Joo Ae Sook?

476
00:31:12,962 --> 00:31:15,162
I don't know. I've never heard that name before.

477
00:31:15,232 --> 00:31:18,602
Is there anything else written besides the name?

478
00:31:19,002 --> 00:31:20,832
Hold on. The baby's date of birth is...

479
00:31:21,062 --> 00:31:23,332
- Yes? - September 11, 2000.

480
00:31:23,702 --> 00:31:25,702
September 11, 2000?

481
00:31:26,102 --> 00:31:27,102
That day is...

482
00:31:28,672 --> 00:31:30,672
Wait, that's the day Eun Seol was born.

483
00:31:31,242 --> 00:31:32,512
The day Eun Seol was born?

484
00:31:32,742 --> 00:31:34,812
Wait, then Joo Ae Sook is...

485
00:31:35,612 --> 00:31:37,112
Eun Seol's biological mother?

486
00:31:40,152 --> 00:31:41,352
Push, just a little more!

487
00:31:42,222 --> 00:31:45,392
Keep going. Just a little more. You're almost there.

488
00:31:45,862 --> 00:31:46,992
You're doing great.

489
00:32:12,082 --> 00:32:16,392
(Mother's Name: Joo Ae Sook, Baby DOB: September 11, 2000)

490
00:32:16,652 --> 00:32:19,162
(Mother's Name: Joo Ae Sook, Baby DOB: September 11, 2000)

491
00:32:41,512 --> 00:32:45,322
(A Trap Called Desire)

492
00:32:45,382 --> 00:32:47,152
Are you happy, Kim Jung Sun?

493
00:32:47,152 --> 00:32:49,122
That spot was supposed to be mine.

494
00:32:49,192 --> 00:32:52,592
But you don't really look like your mother at all.

495
00:32:52,792 --> 00:32:54,992
What do you mean I don't?

496
00:32:55,092 --> 00:32:57,892
Son, let's find Eun Seol's biological mother.

497
00:32:58,062 --> 00:33:00,632
I trusted you from the start, Eun Seol.

498
00:33:00,802 --> 00:33:03,102
I'll always be here rooting for you.

499
00:33:04,532 --> 00:33:06,102
Ms. Park is the real problem.

500
00:33:06,272 --> 00:33:09,142
Director Joo, can you really take care of her for me?

501
00:33:09,212 --> 00:33:11,142
You think I can't handle something like that?

502
00:33:11,372 --> 00:33:12,382
My daughter,

503
00:33:12,882 --> 00:33:13,882
Hae Ra.

504
00:33:14,042 --> 00:33:17,682
You are my greatest masterpiece.
